Lasitan-Cluster
===============

This package provides Lasitan-Cluster, a mesh control plane and agent that
speaks WireGuard over TCP with optional Minecraft protocol camouflage. Both
tunnel ends must use this binary (not kernel WireGuard / stock UDP wireguard-go).

The package only ships two local config examples:

  /etc/lasitan-cluster/lasitan-cluster-master.json.example   Master (control plane)
  /etc/lasitan-cluster/lasitan-cluster-agent.json.example    Agent (tunnel node)

Everything else - VPN addresses, links, routes, port forwards, transport /
MC camouflage settings - is managed in the Master web UI and pushed to
agents over the control connection.

Master
------

A host installed as master cannot also run an agent tunnel.

1. sudo lasitan-cluster install master
   (creates /etc/lasitan-cluster/lasitan-cluster-master.json from the example)
2. Edit /etc/lasitan-cluster/lasitan-cluster-master.json:
     listen, adminPassword, dataDir
3. sudo systemctl restart lasitan-cluster-master
4. Open http://HOST:8443/ and log in with adminPassword
5. The enroll key (a random one is generated on first start) and the
   address pool for new nodes are shown and edited in the web UI.

Agent
-----

1. sudo lasitan-cluster install
   (creates /etc/lasitan-cluster/lasitan-cluster-agent.json from the example)
2. Edit /etc/lasitan-cluster/lasitan-cluster-agent.json:
     {
       "masterUrl": "http://MASTER:8443",
       "key": "<enroll key from the Master web UI>"
     }
   After the first enroll the key is replaced with the node token.
3. sudo systemctl restart lasitan-cluster@lc0

Upgrade
-------

  sudo lasitan-cluster update          # check GitHub Releases and upgrade
  sudo lasitan-cluster update --check  # only report

apt / dpkg upgrades restart running lasitan-cluster@* instances and the Master.

Service management
------------------

  systemctl status lasitan-cluster@lc0        journalctl -u lasitan-cluster@lc0 -f
  systemctl status lasitan-cluster-master     journalctl -u lasitan-cluster-master -f

  sudo lasitan-cluster uninstall [--purge]            # agent
  sudo lasitan-cluster uninstall master [--purge]     # master

install / uninstall / update auto-elevate when not root (sudo -n, pkexec,
then interactive sudo).

Foreground (debug):

  sudo LOG_LEVEL=verbose /usr/bin/lasitan-cluster -f lc0
  sudo /usr/bin/lasitan-cluster master

Paths
-----

  Binary:  /usr/bin/lasitan-cluster
  Config:  /etc/lasitan-cluster/
  Data:    /var/lib/lasitan-cluster/  (Master SQLite mesh.db)
  Units:   /lib/systemd/system/lasitan-cluster@.service
           /lib/systemd/system/lasitan-cluster-master.service
